{
  "dom_id": "step-q182384",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧B)∨A\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |",
  "worked_solution": "First, we complete a truth table for the part in parentheses, $A∧B.$  The statement $A∧B$ is true if both $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nThen, we look at the columns labeled $A∧B$ and $A$ to complete the column $(A∧B)∨A.$ The statement $(A∧B)∨A$ is true if either $A∧B$ is true, $A$ is true, or both $A∧B$ and $A$ are true. \n\nThe completed truth table is shown below:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,A∧B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧B)∨A\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
